; YAML's transducer part: the document's JSON events from the yaml
; grammar's rule passes, for a host that reads parser events (dmog's
; `translate` and `run --grammar yaml`). It is hand-written, since the
; grammar builds its block structure and the relaxed forms it shares with
; jsonic in its actions, which the passes do not show, and every event is
; the one the walk of the grammar's value under its default options gives:
; the options every host that reads a part builds the grammar with, which
; the passes do not carry.
;
; The passes: a `map`'s open and close an object, a flow `list`'s an
; array, and the `val` or `indent` whose open pushes `yamlBlockList`, the
; block sequence, an array that its own close ends; `yamlBlockList` and
; `yamlBlockElem`, the items, pass by. A sequence's mapping, `yamlElemMap`
; (`- a: 1`), opens an object and is replaced by its pairs in the same
; frame, so the close of its last pair, the one whose alternate replaces
; it with nothing, ends the object. A `pair` opened on its key alternate,
; and a `yamlElemPair`, announces its key from its key token (a string's
; value, any other token's source; the token after `?` on an explicit
; key), held until the value begins; a pair opened on a separator with no
; key announces nothing. A `val` yields its scalar at its close, from the
; value the close carries, so that adjacent scalars (`"a" "b"`), an
; implicit list the close replaces the val with `list` for, start the
; array before the first and the list's open starts no second one. An
; undefined value (`a:`, `- a:`, `- `, an alias whose anchor's node is
; still open) is null in a mapping, at the root and as a block sequence's
; item, and nothing in a flow sequence, as the grammar keeps each; a pair
; opened on a key with no value in a flow mapping (`{a, b: c}`) is a null
; member at once, as the grammar stores it; an `indent` opened on a plain
; scalar (`a:` and the scalar on the next line, indented) yields it at its
; close, as a `val` does; an `elem` opened on a separator with no value
; (`[a, , b]`) is a null element; a stream of directives and document
; markers alone (`...`) makes a `stream` pass and no value, null at
; `finish`, as the empty document is.
;
; Anchors and aliases. The lexer reads `&name` and hands it to the val
; that claims it, so no pass carries it; the grammar names it instead in
; that val's counters, `&name`, whose value is the val's own instance
; number, and marks the val with the counter `yamlAnchored`, of the same
; value. A counter passes to the rules below the val with the val's
; number, so the anchored val is the one whose `yamlAnchored` is its own
; `:i`, and its anchors are the `&name` counters of that value.
; From that val's open pass to its close the part keeps the events of its
; value, each with its depth in the value, as they are written; at the
; close a mapping's or a sequence's are recorded under the name, in place
; of the name's earlier record, as the grammar records the node. An alias
; is a token whose value the grammar resolved: a scalar's the val's close
; carries; a collection's are the events recorded under the alias's name,
; written again at the val's close, after checking that the token's value
; is a collection of that kind and size; and an alias read while its
; anchor's node was still open (`&a [*a]`) is undefined, as the grammar
; reads it. Every value the part keeps is held in its state, under
; max_metadata_bytes, past which the run fails with
; RESOURCE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED naming it, and the anchored values are kept for
; the rest of the document, as the grammar keeps them.
;
; Merge keys. A plain `<<` in a mapping (`map`; a sequence's mapping is
; not merged, as the grammar merges none) is no member: the part keeps its
; value's events, a level of their own that recorders see and the output
; does not, until the mapping closes. The grammar folds the members in at
; the map's close, after the passes, keeping the mapping's own keys
; wherever they stand, and names each key it merged in the map's counters,
; `<<key`, on its close pass, with the number of the source it took the
; key from: 1 for the mapping the `<<` names, and for a sequence, the
; place of the mapping among the sequence's mappings, from 1. The part
; finds the members of that mapping, or of each mapping the sequence
; holds, with one sort over the kept events, and writes those the
; counters name, in order, as the mapping's last members. Each key the
; grammar merged is one member the part kept, or the part refuses: a
; source that repeats a key the grammar merged, whose values the grammar
; combines before it merges, keeps the key twice. A quoted `<<` is an
; ordinary key and leaves its mapping unmerged; a mapping that holds both,
; or two plain `<<`, whose values the grammar combines, is refused too.
; The part refuses each in its own words (`fail :unstreamable`,
; STREAMABILITY_UNKNOWN), and a host that reads a part reads such a
; document whole.
;
; What the tree contract after the part refuses is read whole the same
; way: a stream of several documents, whose second root follows the
; first, and a mapping that repeats a key, whose values the grammar
; combines, where the part writes the member twice. Over the 626 inputs
; of `test/spec/*.tsv` that are not error rows, the part writes what the
; walk writes for 581; it refuses 6 itself, merge sources that repeat a
; key the grammar merged, and the tree contract refuses the other 39 (18
; streams of several documents, 21 repeated keys). Over the YAML Test
; Suite's 308 cases that are not error cases, the reader reads 287, and
; the part writes what the walk writes for 269 of them; the other 18 are
; streams of several documents.
;
; The state is [stack carry rooted pending held], held [levels anchors
; merges]. The stack holds a marker per open rule whose close will come,
; innermost last: :object for a map (:merge-object once a merge key opens
; in it, :quoted-object once a quoted `<<` does), :array for a flow list,
; :block-array for the val or indent whose open pushed the block list,
; :elem-object for a yamlElemMap, :leaf for a val that pushed nothing,
; [:alias name shape] for a val whose token is an alias to a collection,
; :merge-pair for a merge key's pair, and :skip for any other rule. carry
; says whether a val's close made an implicit list, so the list's open
; starts no array; rooted, whether a value has begun; pending, the key a
; pair announced whose value has not begun, or missing. A level is [sink
; recorders]: the sink is :out, the output, at the root, or a collector of
; a merge key's value; a recorder is [i names collector] for an open
; anchored val; a collector is [depth started done items], the events
; kept with their depths. anchors holds [name items] per recorded
; anchor, merges the candidates of each open merging mapping, innermost
; last. Without anchors and merge keys nothing grows with the document's
; length, only with its nesting.

def yaml-transduce-has-key [groups]
  match (count (filter (fn [g] (match g (case "key" true) (case _ false))) groups))
    case 0 false
    case _ true

def yaml-transduce-has-null [groups]
  match (count (filter (fn [g] (match g (case "null" true) (case _ false))) groups))
    case 0 false
    case _ true

def yaml-transduce-has-yaml [groups]
  match (count (filter (fn [g] (match g (case "yaml" true) (case _ false))) groups))
    case 0 false
    case _ true

def yaml-transduce-key-text [token]
  match (kind (get :val token))
    case :string (get :val token)
    case _ (get :src token)

; Whether a key token is the merge key, a plain `<<`; and whether it is a
; quoted `<<`, which is a string, so an ordinary key.
def yaml-transduce-merge-key [token]
  match (get :name token)
    case "#TX" (equal (get :val token) "<<")
    case _ false

def yaml-transduce-quoted-merge-key [token]
  match (get :name token)
    case "#ST" (equal (get :val token) "<<")
    case _ false

; The token a pair's open announces its key with: the first on the key
; alternate, the one after `?` on an explicit key's (`{? a : 1}`), none
; on any other (a separator with no key).
def yaml-transduce-key-token [rule]
  match (yaml-transduce-has-key (yaml-transduce-groups rule))
    case true (transduce-token 0 rule)
    case _
      match (transduce-token 0 rule)
        case missing missing
        case token
          match (get :name token)
            case "#QM" (transduce-token 1 rule)
            case _ missing

; The token a sequence's pair (yamlElemPair) announces its key with: its
; first, or the one after `?` on an explicit key's.
def yaml-transduce-elem-key-token [rule]
  match (transduce-token 0 rule)
    case missing missing
    case token
      match (get :name token)
        case "#QM" (transduce-token 1 rule)
        case _ token

def yaml-transduce-groups [rule]
  match (get :alt rule)
    case missing []
    case alt (get :g alt)

def yaml-transduce-pushes [rule]
  match (get :alt rule)
    case missing ""
    case alt (get :p alt)

def yaml-transduce-replaces [rule]
  match (get :alt rule)
    case missing ""
    case alt (get :r alt)

; The innermost container the stack holds, or missing at the root.
def yaml-transduce-container [stack]
  let [containers (filter (fn [m] (match m (case :object true) (case :merge-object true) (case :quoted-object true) (case :array true) (case :block-array true) (case :elem-object true) (case _ false))) stack)]
    match (count containers)
      case 0 missing
      case _ (top containers)

; A value's pieces, after the key pending for it, if one is.
def yaml-transduce-value [pending pieces]
  match pending
    case missing pieces
    case name (push-all pieces [(key name)])

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Pieces and collectors
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; What a pass writes is a vector of pieces: an event, or a run, [:run
; offset items], events kept with their depths, which a collector places
; at its own depth and the offset. A collector keeps one value's events
; as [depth event] items, the value's start and end at depth 0; it skips
; a key before the value begins, which is the value's parent's.

def yaml-transduce-collector [0 false false []]

def yaml-transduce-shut [c e items]
  [c true (equal c 0) (push [c e] items)]

def yaml-transduce-collect-event [c started items e]
  match started
    case false
      match e
        case object-start [1 true false [[0 e]]]
        case array-start [1 true false [[0 e]]]
        case (scalar v) [0 true true [[0 e]]]
        case _ [c false false items]
    case _
      match e
        case object-start [(inc c) true false (push [c e] items)]
        case array-start [(inc c) true false (push [c e] items)]
        case object-end (yaml-transduce-shut (sub c 1) e items)
        case array-end (yaml-transduce-shut (sub c 1) e items)
        case _ [c true false (push [c e] items)]

; A run is a whole value, or a mapping's members (offset -1, a key at depth
; 1 in it), which leave the collector's depth as it was.
def yaml-transduce-collect-run [c started items run]
  match run
    case [:run off more]
      let [base (add c off)
           moved (map (fn [p] (match p (case [d e] [(add d base) e]))) more)]
        match started
          case false [0 true true moved]
          case _ [c true false (push-all moved items)]

def yaml-transduce-collect [coll piece]
  match coll
    case [c started true items] coll
    case [c started done items]
      match (kind piece)
        case :vector (yaml-transduce-collect-run c started items piece)
        case _ (yaml-transduce-collect-event c started items piece)

; A piece's events, as the output takes them.
def yaml-transduce-plain [piece]
  match (kind piece)
    case :vector
      match piece
        case [:run off items] (map (fn [p] (match p (case [d e] e))) items)
    case _ [piece]

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Anchors
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; Whether a pass is an anchored val's: its `yamlAnchored` is its own
; instance number.
def yaml-transduce-anchored-val [rule]
  match (get :name rule)
    case "val"
      match (get :n rule)
        case missing false
        case n (equal (get "yamlAnchored" n) (get :i rule))
    case _ false

; The anchors an anchored val's pass names: each counter `&name` whose
; value is the val's instance number.
def yaml-transduce-anchor-names [rule]
  let [n (get :n rule)]
    map (fn [k] (get-path (path 1) (first-split "&" k)))
      filter (fn [k] (if (starts-with "&" k) (equal (get k n) (get :i rule)) false)) (keys n)

; An anchored val opens: a recorder of its value, in the innermost level.
def yaml-transduce-record-open [held rule]
  match (yaml-transduce-anchored-val rule)
    case false held
    case _
      match held
        case [levels anchors merges]
          match (top levels)
            case [sink recorders]
              [(push [sink (push [(get :i rule) (yaml-transduce-anchor-names rule) yaml-transduce-collector] recorders)] (pop levels)) anchors merges]

def yaml-transduce-unnamed [names name]
  match (count (filter (fn [n] (equal n name)) names))
    case 0 true
    case _ false

; The anchors once a val that names `names` recorded its value: a
; mapping's or a sequence's events under each name, in place of the
; name's earlier record; for a scalar, which the token of an alias
; carries, no record.
def yaml-transduce-anchored [anchors names coll]
  let [rest (filter (fn [a] (match a (case [name items] (yaml-transduce-unnamed names name)))) anchors)]
    match coll
      case [c started true items]
        match (get-path (path 0) items)
          case [0 object-start] (push-all (map (fn [name] [name items]) names) rest)
          case [0 array-start] (push-all (map (fn [name] [name items]) names) rest)
          case _ rest
      case _ rest

; An anchored val closes, after what its close writes: its recorder, the
; innermost of the innermost level, is recorded.
def yaml-transduce-record-close [state rule]
  match (yaml-transduce-anchored-val rule)
    case false state
    case _
      match state
        case [stack carry rooted pending [levels anchors merges]]
          match (top levels)
            case [sink recorders]
              match recorders
                case [] (fail :protocol-order "an anchored value closed that did not open, which the passes never make")
                case _
                  match (top recorders)
                    case [i kept coll]
                      match (equal i (get :i rule))
                        case true [stack carry rooted pending [(push [sink (pop recorders)] (pop levels)) (yaml-transduce-anchored anchors kept coll) merges]]
                        case _ (fail :protocol-order "an anchored value closed inside another, which the passes never make")

; The events recorded under an anchor's name, or missing.
def yaml-transduce-recording [name anchors]
  let [found (filter (fn [a] (match a (case [n items] (equal n name)))) anchors)]
    match found
      case [] missing
      case _
        match (top found)
          case [n items] items

; What an alias token's value is: the grammar's marker of an anchor whose
; node was still open when the alias was read, or a collection of a kind
; and a size, which the events recorded under the name must have.
def yaml-transduce-shape [val]
  match (kind val)
    case :vector [:array (count val)]
    case _
      match (get "__yamlAlias" val)
        case missing [:object (count (keys val))]
        case _ [:marker 0]

; How many members or elements recorded events hold.
def yaml-transduce-size [items]
  match (get-path (path 0) items)
    case [0 object-start] (count (filter (fn [p] (match p (case [1 (key k)] true) (case _ false))) items))
    case _ (count (filter (fn [p] (match p (case [1 (scalar v)] true) (case [1 object-start] true) (case [1 array-start] true) (case _ false))) items))

def yaml-transduce-fits [shape items]
  match [shape (get-path (path 0) items)]
    case [[:marker n] _] true
    case [[:array n] [0 array-start]] (equal n (yaml-transduce-size items))
    case [[:object n] [0 object-start]] (equal n (yaml-transduce-size items))
    case _ false

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Routing
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

def yaml-transduce-keep [recorder piece]
  match recorder
    case [i names coll] [i names (yaml-transduce-collect coll piece)]

; One piece through the innermost level: each recorder there keeps it, and
; its sink takes it, the output or a merge key's collector.
def yaml-transduce-route [routed piece]
  match routed
    case [[stack carry rooted pending [levels anchors merges]] outputs]
      match (top levels)
        case [sink recorders]
          let [kept (map (fn [r] (yaml-transduce-keep r piece)) recorders)]
            match sink
              case :out [[stack carry rooted pending [(push [sink kept] (pop levels)) anchors merges]] (push-all (yaml-transduce-plain piece) outputs)]
              case _ [[stack carry rooted pending [(push [(yaml-transduce-collect sink piece) kept] (pop levels)) anchors merges]] outputs]

def yaml-transduce-routed [routed]
  match routed
    case [state outputs] (transition state outputs)

; A pass's pieces, routed in order: at most four, a key, an implicit
; list's start, and a value's one or two.
def yaml-transduce-routes [state pieces]
  match pieces
    case [] (transition state [])
    case [a] (yaml-transduce-routed (yaml-transduce-route [state []] a))
    case [a b] (yaml-transduce-routed (yaml-transduce-route (yaml-transduce-route [state []] a) b))
    case [a b c] (yaml-transduce-routed (yaml-transduce-route (yaml-transduce-route (yaml-transduce-route [state []] a) b) c))
    case [a b c d] (yaml-transduce-routed (yaml-transduce-route (yaml-transduce-route (yaml-transduce-route (yaml-transduce-route [state []] a) b) c) d))
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "a rule pass made more pieces than the part writes for one")

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Merge keys
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; A merge key's value is collected whole, as [depth event] items, and held
; until its mapping closes, whose counters name each key the grammar
; merged and the source it took it from. Its members are found by one
; sort over its items, never by a search per member, so finding them
; costs what sorting the items does, however many members there are.

def yaml-transduce-shallower [d depth]
  match (compare d depth)
    case :less true
    case _ false

def yaml-transduce-not-deeper [d depth]
  match (compare d depth)
    case :greater false
    case _ true

; Whether an item bounds a member when the members' keys stand at
; `depth`: such a key, which starts one, or any item above them, which
; ends the last.
def yaml-transduce-bound [depth item]
  match item
    case [d (key k)] (yaml-transduce-not-deeper d depth)
    case [d e] (yaml-transduce-shallower d depth)

; Four times a number, which a mark sorts as; a place sorts as one more.
def yaml-transduce-quadruple [x]
  let [twice (add x x)]
    add twice twice

; Whether the number at i of a sorted whole of marks and places is a
; mark's: a mark m sorts as 4m, just before 4m + 1, its own place's,
; where a place's number is followed by the next mark's or place's, three
; or four more.
def yaml-transduce-mark [i all]
  match (get-path (path (inc i)) all)
    case missing false
    case next (equal next (inc (get-path (path i) all)))

; For each place 0 to n - 1 (`places`, the indices of a vector of n
; items), the index in `marks`, places in ascending order, of the last
; mark at or before it, or -1. One sort answers every place: the marks
; and the places sort together, a mark just before its own place, so the
; place k stands after the k places before it and the marks at or before
; it.
def yaml-transduce-owners [marks places]
  let [all (sort (push-all (map (fn [x] (inc (yaml-transduce-quadruple x))) places) (map (fn [m] (yaml-transduce-quadruple m)) marks)))
       at (filter (fn [i] (if (yaml-transduce-mark i all) false true)) (indices all))]
    map (fn [k] (sub (sub (get-path (path k) at) k) 1)) (indices at)

def yaml-transduce-mapping-start [item]
  match item
    case [1 object-start] true
    case _ false

; The number of the source each bound (`marked`, the items that bound)
; stands in: 1 in a mapping; in a sequence, the place of its mapping among
; the sequence's mappings, from 1, as the grammar counts them (0 before
; the first).
def yaml-transduce-sources [depth marked]
  match depth
    case 1 (map (fn [b] 1) marked)
    case _
      let [starts (filter (fn [p] (yaml-transduce-mapping-start (get-path (path p) marked))) (indices marked))]
        map (fn [o] (add o 1)) (yaml-transduce-owners starts (indices marked))

; Whether a bound is the key of a member the grammar merged from source
; s: its mapping's counter `<<key` names that source.
def yaml-transduce-takes [depth item s n]
  match item
    case [d (key k)] (if (equal d depth) (equal (get (string-join "" ["<<" k]) n) s) false)
    case _ false

def yaml-transduce-key-name [item]
  match item
    case [d (key k)] k

; What a merge key's value brings to its mapping, which closed with the
; counters n: [names items], the names of the members the grammar took
; from it and their events, in order, each key moved to depth 1. Every
; item belongs to the last bound at or before it, so a member the grammar
; took keeps its items, and nothing else is kept.
def yaml-transduce-merge-members [depth items n]
  let [bounds (filter (fn [x] (yaml-transduce-bound depth (get-path (path x) items))) (indices items))
       marked (map (fn [b] (get-path (path b) items)) bounds)
       sources (yaml-transduce-sources depth marked)
       taken (map (fn [p] (yaml-transduce-takes depth (get-path (path p) marked) (get-path (path p) sources) n)) (indices marked))
       keeps (map (fn [o] (get-path (path o) taken)) (yaml-transduce-owners bounds (indices items)))
       kept (filter (fn [x] (get-path (path x) keeps)) (indices items))]
    [(map (fn [p] (yaml-transduce-key-name (get-path (path p) marked))) (filter (fn [p] (get-path (path p) taken)) (indices marked)))
     (map (fn [x] (match (get-path (path x) items) (case [d e] [(sub d (sub depth 1)) e]))) kept)]

; A mapping's members, keys at depth 1, or the members of each mapping a
; sequence holds, keys at depth 2; nothing from any other value.
def yaml-transduce-merge-run [items n]
  match (get-path (path 0) items)
    case [0 object-start] (yaml-transduce-merge-members 1 items n)
    case [0 array-start] (yaml-transduce-merge-members 2 items n)
    case _ [[] []]

; A merge key's pair opens in a mapping: the mapping merges, and the
; pair's value is collected in a level of its own, not written.
def yaml-transduce-merge-open [rest carry held]
  match held
    case [levels anchors merges]
      transition [(push :merge-pair (push :merge-object rest)) carry true missing [(push [yaml-transduce-collector []] levels) anchors (push [] merges)]] []

; A collector's items once it holds a whole value, or none.
def yaml-transduce-collected [coll]
  match coll
    case [c started true items] items
    case _ []

; A merge key's pair closes: its value's events are held for its
; mapping's close.
def yaml-transduce-merge-taken [rest carry rooted pending held]
  match held
    case [levels anchors merges]
      match (top levels)
        case [collected recorders]
          transition [rest carry rooted pending [(pop levels) anchors (push (yaml-transduce-collected collected) (pop merges))]] []

; The keys the grammar merged into a mapping, which its close pass names
; in its counters, each `<<` and the key.
def yaml-transduce-merged-keys [n]
  map (fn [k] (get-path (path 1) (first-split "<<" k)))
    filter (fn [k] (starts-with "<<" k)) (keys n)

; A merging mapping closes: the members the grammar took, in order, then
; its end. Each key the grammar merged is one member the part kept, or the
; part refuses: a source that repeats a key, whose values the grammar
; combines, keeps the key twice.
def yaml-transduce-merged [rest carry rooted pending held rule]
  match held
    case [levels anchors merges]
      let [n (get-or :n (record) rule)]
        match (yaml-transduce-merge-run (top merges) n)
          case [names items]
            match (equal (sort names) (sort (yaml-transduce-merged-keys n)))
              case true (transition [rest carry rooted pending [levels anchors (pop merges)]] [[:run -1 items] object-end])
              case _ (fail :unstreamable "a merge whose source repeats a key the grammar merged, whose values it combines, or whose members the part did not keep")

def yaml-transduce-unmerged [why]
  fail :unstreamable why

; A pair's key in a mapping: a plain `<<` opens the merge; a quoted one is
; a member that leaves the mapping unmerged; the two together, or a
; second plain one, are combined by the grammar, which the part refuses.
def yaml-transduce-pair-key [stack carry rooted held token]
  let [name (yaml-transduce-key-text token)]
    match [(yaml-transduce-merge-key token) (yaml-transduce-quoted-merge-key token) (top stack)]
      case [true false :object] (yaml-transduce-merge-open (pop stack) carry held)
      case [true false :merge-object] (yaml-transduce-unmerged "a mapping with a second merge key, whose values the grammar combines")
      case [true false :quoted-object] (yaml-transduce-unmerged "a merge key in a mapping that holds a quoted <<, which the grammar leaves unmerged")
      case [false true :merge-object] (yaml-transduce-unmerged "a quoted << in a mapping with a merge key, which the grammar leaves unmerged")
      case [false true :object] (transition [(push :skip (push :quoted-object (pop stack))) carry rooted name held] [])
      case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted name held] [])

; A key with no value in a flow mapping (`{a, b: c}`, `{? a, b: c}`): a
; null member at once, as the grammar stores it; a plain `<<` merges null,
; which brings nothing.
def yaml-transduce-null-member [stack carry pending held token]
  let [name (yaml-transduce-key-text token)
       member (yaml-transduce-value pending [(key name) (scalar null)])]
    match held
      case [levels anchors merges]
        match [(yaml-transduce-merge-key token) (yaml-transduce-quoted-merge-key token) (top stack)]
          case [true false :object] (transition [(push :skip (push :merge-object (pop stack))) carry true pending [levels anchors (push [] merges)]] [])
          case [true false :merge-object] (yaml-transduce-unmerged "a mapping with a second merge key, whose values the grammar combines")
          case [true false :quoted-object] (yaml-transduce-unmerged "a merge key in a mapping that holds a quoted <<, which the grammar leaves unmerged")
          case [false true :merge-object] (yaml-transduce-unmerged "a quoted << in a mapping with a merge key, which the grammar leaves unmerged")
          case [false true :object] (transition [(push :skip (push :quoted-object (pop stack))) carry true missing held] member)
          case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry true missing held] member)

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; The rule passes
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------

; A val whose token's value is a collection: an alias, whose name is its
; source after the `*`.
def yaml-transduce-alias-open [stack carry pending held token]
  match (first-split "*" (get :src token))
    case ["" name] (transition [(push [:alias name (yaml-transduce-shape (get :val token))] stack) carry true pending held] [])
    case _ (fail :unstreamable "a collection in a token that is no alias, whose events the passes do not show")

; A val that pushed nothing: a leaf, or an alias to a collection.
def yaml-transduce-leaf-open [stack carry pending held rule]
  match (transduce-token 0 rule)
    case missing (transition [(push :leaf stack) carry true pending held] [])
    case token
      match (kind (get :val token))
        case :record (yaml-transduce-alias-open stack carry pending held token)
        case :vector (yaml-transduce-alias-open stack carry pending held token)
        case _ (transition [(push :leaf stack) carry true pending held] [])

def yaml-transduce-val-open [stack carry pending held rule]
  match (yaml-transduce-pushes rule)
    case "yamlBlockList" (transition [(push :block-array stack) carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [array-start]))
    case "" (yaml-transduce-leaf-open stack carry pending held rule)
    case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry true pending held] [])

; A pair whose alternate pushes nothing: on the grammar's own alternates
; for a key with no value in a flow mapping, which consume the key (the
; one after `?` on an explicit key's), the member; on a separator with no
; key, or the end of the source, nothing.
def yaml-transduce-pair-without-value [stack carry rooted pending held rule]
  match (yaml-transduce-has-yaml (yaml-transduce-groups rule))
    case true
      match (yaml-transduce-elem-key-token rule)
        case missing (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])
        case token (yaml-transduce-null-member stack carry pending held token)
    case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])

def yaml-transduce-open [stack carry rooted pending held rule]
  match (get :name rule)
    case "map" (transition [(push :object stack) carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [object-start]))
    case "list"
      match carry
        case true (transition [(push :array stack) false true pending held] [])
        case _ (transition [(push :array stack) carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [array-start]))
    case "val" (yaml-transduce-val-open stack carry pending held rule)
    case "indent"
      match (yaml-transduce-pushes rule)
        case "yamlBlockList" (transition [(push :block-array stack) carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [array-start]))
        case "" (transition [(push :leaf stack) carry true pending held] [])
        case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])
    case "pair"
      match (yaml-transduce-pushes rule)
        case "" (yaml-transduce-pair-without-value stack carry rooted pending held rule)
        case _
          match (yaml-transduce-key-token rule)
            case missing (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])
            case token (yaml-transduce-pair-key stack carry rooted held token)
    case "elem"
      match (yaml-transduce-has-null (yaml-transduce-groups rule))
        case true (transition [(push :skip stack) carry true pending held] [(scalar null)])
        case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])
    case "yamlElemMap"
      match (yaml-transduce-replaces rule)
        case "yamlElemPair" (transition [(push :elem-object stack) carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [object-start]))
        case _ (transition [(push :object stack) carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [object-start]))
    case "yamlElemPair"
      match (yaml-transduce-elem-key-token rule)
        case missing (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])
        case token (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted (yaml-transduce-key-text token) held] [])
    case "stream"
      match (yaml-transduce-replaces rule)
        case "stream" (transition [stack carry rooted pending held] [])
        case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])
    case _ (transition [(push :skip stack) carry rooted pending held] [])

; An undefined value: null in a mapping, a sequence's mapping included, at
; the root and as a block sequence's item; nothing in a flow sequence, as
; the grammar keeps each.
def yaml-transduce-undefined [rest carry pending held]
  match (yaml-transduce-container rest)
    case :array (transition [rest carry true missing held] [])
    case _ (transition [rest carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [(scalar null)]))

; A val's value at its close; a close whose alternate replaces the val
; with list is the first element of an implicit list, which starts before
; it.
def yaml-transduce-yield [rest carry pending held rule pieces]
  match (yaml-transduce-replaces rule)
    case "list" (transition [rest true true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending (push-all pieces [array-start])))
    case _ (transition [rest carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending pieces))

def yaml-transduce-leaf [rest carry pending held rule]
  match (get :value rule)
    case missing (yaml-transduce-undefined rest carry pending held)
    case value
      match (yaml-transduce-replaces rule)
        case "list" (transition [rest true true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [array-start (scalar value)]))
        case _ (transition [rest carry true missing held] (yaml-transduce-value pending [(scalar value)]))

def yaml-transduce-unrecorded [rest carry pending held shape]
  match shape
    case [:marker n] (yaml-transduce-undefined rest carry pending held)
    case _ (fail :unstreamable "an alias to a collection whose events the part did not keep")

; An alias's val closes: the scalar its close carries, or the events
; recorded under its name, written again.
def yaml-transduce-alias-close [rest carry pending held rule name shape]
  match (get :value rule)
    case missing
      match held
        case [levels anchors merges]
          match (yaml-transduce-recording name anchors)
            case missing (yaml-transduce-unrecorded rest carry pending held shape)
            case items
              match (yaml-transduce-fits shape items)
                case true (yaml-transduce-yield rest carry pending held rule [[:run 0 items]])
                case _ (fail :unstreamable "an alias whose value is not the events its anchor's node gave")
    case value (yaml-transduce-yield rest carry pending held rule [(scalar value)])

def yaml-transduce-close [stack carry rooted pending held rule]
  let [rest (pop stack)]
    match (top stack)
      case :leaf (yaml-transduce-leaf rest carry pending held rule)
      case [:alias name shape] (yaml-transduce-alias-close rest carry pending held rule name shape)
      case :object (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [object-end])
      case :quoted-object (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [object-end])
      case :merge-object (yaml-transduce-merged rest carry rooted pending held rule)
      case :array (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [array-end])
      case :block-array (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [array-end])
      case :elem-object (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [object-end])
      case :merge-pair (yaml-transduce-merge-taken rest carry rooted pending held)
      case _
        match (get :name rule)
          case "yamlElemPair"
            match (yaml-transduce-replaces rule)
              case "yamlElemPair" (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [])
              case _
                match (top rest)
                  case :elem-object (transition [(pop rest) carry rooted pending held] [object-end])
                  case _ (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [])
          case _ (transition [rest carry rooted pending held] [])

; An open pass: an anchored val's recorder opens before its value's first
; event.
def yaml-transduce-routed-pass [result]
  match result
    case (transition state pieces) (yaml-transduce-routes state pieces)

; Nothing held: no anchored value has been recorded or is open, and no
; merge key's mapping is open.
def yaml-transduce-unheld [[[:out []]] [] []]

; An open pass with something held, or of an anchored val: its pieces are
; routed through the innermost level.
def yaml-transduce-kept-open [stack carry rooted pending held rule]
  yaml-transduce-routed-pass (yaml-transduce-open stack carry rooted pending (yaml-transduce-record-open held rule) rule)

def yaml-transduce-kept-close [stack carry rooted pending held rule]
  match (yaml-transduce-routed-pass (yaml-transduce-close stack carry rooted pending held rule))
    case (transition routed outputs) (transition (yaml-transduce-record-close routed rule) outputs)

; An open pass with nothing held: its pieces are its events, unless it is
; an anchored val's.
def yaml-transduce-unheld-open [stack carry rooted pending rule]
  match (get :name rule)
    case "val"
      match (equal (get "yamlAnchored" (get :n rule)) (get :i rule))
        case true (yaml-transduce-kept-open stack carry rooted pending yaml-transduce-unheld rule)
        case _ (yaml-transduce-val-open stack carry pending yaml-transduce-unheld rule)
    case _ (yaml-transduce-open stack carry rooted pending yaml-transduce-unheld rule)

; A pass with nothing held writes its pieces, which are events, as they
; are; with something held, each piece is routed.
def yaml-transduce-step [state pass]
  match state
    case [stack carry rooted pending [[[:out []]] [] []]]
      match pass
        case (open rule) (yaml-transduce-unheld-open stack carry rooted pending rule)
        case (close rule) (yaml-transduce-close stack carry rooted pending yaml-transduce-unheld rule)
    case [stack carry rooted pending held]
      match pass
        case (open rule) (yaml-transduce-kept-open stack carry rooted pending held rule)
        case (close rule) (yaml-transduce-kept-close stack carry rooted pending held rule)

def yaml-transduce-finish [state]
  match state
    case [[] carry false pending held] [(scalar null)]
    case [[] carry true pending held] []
    case _ (fail :protocol-order "the rule passes ended inside a container, which a tree's never do")

def yaml-transduce [input]
  as-events (scan-emit [[] false false missing [[[:out []]] [] []]] yaml-transduce-step yaml-transduce-finish (parser-events input))
